%
%  Ex_FormationFlying_SSO_FEEP
%
%  Delta-V budget for a two-satellite formation in a sun-synchronous orbit
%  (SSO) over 5 years, with FEEP (field emission electric propulsion)
%  thrusters. FEEP can only fire continuously at low thrust, so there are no
%  impulsive burns anywhere in this script: every manoeuvre is a finite burn,
%  throttled with the thruster DutyCycle and held for a whole control cycle.
%
%  FORMATION REQUIREMENT (RTN frame centred on Sat1, Sat2 relative to Sat1)
%     Along-track (T) separation :  300 ... 800 km
%     Normal (N) separation      :  200 km (amplitude, see below)
%
%  The normal separation is created with a RAAN (LTAN) offset between the two
%  planes, NOT with an inclination difference. Both satellites have the same
%  a, e, i, so their J2 nodal precession is identical (both are sun-
%  synchronous) and the offset is passively stable. A constant 200 km N offset
%  is not possible in orbit, so "200 km normal" is taken as the amplitude of
%  the N component, which swings +/-200 km over each orbit:
%        A_N = a * sqrt( di^2 + (sin(i) * dRAAN)^2 )  =  NAmp
%
%  ASSUMPTIONS (all editable below)
%     560 km circular SSO, LTAN 10:30, start 01 Jan 2027, 5 years (1826 days)
%     2 identical 400 kg satellites (395 kg dry + 5 kg propellant), Cd 3.0,
%     drag area 4.5 m^2 each (SRP area 4.5 m^2, Cr 1.3)
%     FEEP: 1 mN maximum thrust per thruster, Isp 2800 s, one
%     prograde and two out-of-plane (+N / -N) thrusters per satellite, power
%     never limits thrust
%     Gravity 8x8, Sun + Moon, SRP, NRLMSISE-00 drag with the Schatten (MSFC)
%     solar-cycle prediction: +2 sigma (the 95th percentile of AD10 5.9) for the
%     beginning of life and the operations, nominal (50th percentile) at the end
%     of life. Cd 3.0 during the operations and 2.2 at the end of life (AD10 5.2).
%     AcqOn = 1 (default): both satellites are released at exactly the same
%     position and the formation is built by a phasing manoeuvre (below); its
%     delta-V is part of the budget. AcqOn = 0: they start in their slots.
%
%  STANDARDS
%     The delta-V and propellant budget follows the ESA guidelines EOP-FM/2024-07-177
%     (AD10): contributors per phase (Table 1), finite burns for electric
%     propulsion, Cd, solar-activity percentiles, margin policy, 1 % residual and
%     2 % uncertainty of the tank, iteration on the propellant mass (the last
%     three in plot_formation_results.py). The end of life follows ESSB-ST-U-007
%     (5.4.2.3: natural decay shorter than 5 years from the end of life). What this
%     script covers and what needs other tools is listed in
%     Ex_FormationFlying_SSO_FEEP_compliance.md.
%
%  CONTROL (one cycle = 15 orbits, about 1.000 day)
%     1. Altitude : each satellite tracks a target mean SMA with a PI law on
%                   continuous prograde thrust (drag make-up; the integral
%                   term learns the drag acceleration).
%     2. Along-track : when T leaves [TLow, THigh] a drift back towards the
%                   centre is commanded, then stopped at TCenter. Drift rate
%                   is measured from T, and the SMA offset needed to get the
%                   commanded rate is split between the satellites (the
%                   thrusters are prograde only, so the one that has to be
%                   higher is raised).
%     3. Inclination : HoldSSO = 1: each satellite holds the mean inclination
%                   that gives exactly the sun-synchronous nodal rate. When the
%                   error exceeds iDead, both do an out-of-plane campaign with
%                   sign(cos(u)) thrust (flipped at the polar points).
%                   HoldSSO = 0: no absolute control; the inclination of Sat2
%                   relative to Sat1 is kept (campaigns when it is off by more
%                   than iDeadRel), each satellite doing half of the change so
%                   that both use about the same propellant, and the two planes
%                   keep precessing together.
%                   In both cases the RAAN offset is trimmed with a small
%                   differential inclination if the N amplitude has drifted.
%     0. Acquisition (AcqOn = 1, first months): Sat1 is raised by a small SMA
%                   offset so that Sat2 drifts ahead at VAcq km/day (the same
%                   relative-drift law as 2.); the drift is stopped TLeadAcq km
%                   before TCenter and left to decay with drag. At the same time
%                   Sat2 is held diAcq above Sat1 in inclination (Sat1 goes down and
%                   Sat2 up by half of it each, so both burn the same), which makes
%                   the node of Sat2 run ahead (d(RAAN rate)/di = 0.128 deg/day per deg). The
%                   offset is removed when the RAAN offset predicted for the end
%                   of that ramp reaches dRaan; the slow trim of 3. finishes the
%                   job. Normal separation costs delta-V x time = const: a larger
%                   diAcq is faster and costs proportionally more. Results are
%                   judged (TMin/TMax, nOutT, ...) after the acquisition ends.
%     4. End of life (EolOn = 1, after the last cycle): both satellites are
%                   lowered with retrograde thrusters at full thrust: clearance of
%                   the operational orbit (SMA drop of dAClear = 5 km, AD10 6.3.2),
%                   then disposal to a mean altitude of HDisp. The natural decay
%                   from there is propagated (Cd 2.2, 50th percentile) until
%                   re-entry; it must be shorter than 5 years (ESSB-ST-U-007
%                   5.4.2.3). formation_eol_lifetime.py repeats that check for
%                   start epochs through a full solar cycle (ESSB 6.2.f) to choose
%                   HDisp.
%     The controller uses Brouwer-Lyddane mean elements referred to the
%     true-of-date equator, averaged over the 15 orbits of the cycle.
%
%  DELTA-V ACCOUNTING
%     Integrated from thrust/mass for every burn, separately for the
%     tangential (altitude + along-track) and normal (inclination) thrusters,
%     and cross-checked against the rocket equation from the propellant used
%     (dvRkt1/2 must equal dvT + dvN of the same satellite).
%
%  OUTPUT (GMAT output folder)
%     FormationSSO_FEEP_Daily.txt     one row per control cycle
%     FormationSSO_FEEP_Summary.txt   delta-V budget and compliance summary
%        dvT1/dvN1/dvT2/dvN2 : tangential / normal delta-V of Sat1 / Sat2, m/s
%        dvTot               : total for the formation, m/s
%        TMin/TMax           : along-track separation extremes, km
%        ANMin/ANMax         : normal-separation amplitude extremes, km
%        nOutT/nOutN         : cycles outside 300..800 km / 180..220 km
%        epMax               : largest epoch difference between the satellites, s
%        tAcq                : day the acquisition ended (0 if AcqOn = 0)
%        dvAcqT/N1,2         : delta-V used up to then (included in dvT/dvN)
%        dvNo1/2, dvNf1/2    : normal delta-V after the acquisition: sun-synchronous
%                              hold (out-of-plane orbit control) / formation
%        dvClr1/2, dvDisp1/2 : end of life: clearance, disposal, m/s (not in dvTot)
%        aDispT, life1/2, hEnd1/2 : disposal SMA (km), days to re-entry, final altitude
%        mPropEol, dvRktEol  : propellant and rocket-equation delta-V of the end of life
%     The Daily file has a last column acq (1 while the acquisition runs).
%
%  REFERENCE RESULTS (GMAT R2026a, 560 km, 400 kg, 1 mN, Isp 2800 s, Cd 3.0, 4.5 m^2, 5 years,
%  start 01 Jan 2027 with both satellites at the same point, delta-V in m/s)
%                              Sat1 tang  Sat1 norm  Sat2 tang  Sat2 norm  Formation
%   HoldSSO = 0 (default: the orbit plane is allowed to drift)
%     +2 sigma, 95th percentile      9.6       22.2        9.6       22.2       63.6
%     Schatten nominal               7.0       22.2        7.0       22.2       58.4
%   HoldSSO = 1 (sun-synchronous inclination and LTAN held)
%     +2 sigma, 95th percentile      9.7       53.4        9.7       51.7      124.5
%     Schatten nominal               7.1       53.4        7.1       51.8      119.3
%   tang = altitude + along-track, norm = inclination / node control. Both satellites
%   share the relative inclination changes, so they use the same delta-V and about
%   the same propellant (0.46 / 0.46 kg with HoldSSO = 0, 0.92 / 0.89 kg with
%   HoldSSO = 1; 5 kg tanks). The totals include the acquisition: 179 days, 46.2
%   m/s for the formation at +2 sigma (23.1 per satellite; 44.8 at the nominal
%   activity). The inclination ramps are thrust limited: with diAcq = 0.05 deg it
%   takes 285 days and 25.6 m/s, with 0.20 deg 192 days and 85.6 m/s (nominal).
%   End of life, each satellite, not in the figures above: clearance 2.7 + disposal
%   55.5 m/s down to 450 km, 0.85 kg of propellant. At 1 mN the descent lasts about
%   270 days; the natural decay from 450 km then takes 1.4 years (2.1 years from the
%   end of life; limit 5 years; 4.7 years for the worst of 11 end-of-life epochs,
%   see formation_eol_lifetime.py --descent-days 270). 460 km would take 5.2 years
%   at worst.
%   Launch delay (HoldSSO = 0, +2 sigma, formation delta-V without end of life):
%   1 year 61.0, 2 years 76.2, 3 years 111.1, 4 years 153.0, 5 years 187.1 m/s.
%   After the acquisition the along-track separation stays within 322..606 km (limit
%   50..1000 km) and the N amplitude within 198..208 km in all cases. The prograde
%   thruster fires 1 to 5 % of the time (up to 34 % for a launch 5 years late).
%   With HoldSSO = 0 the inclination falls from 97.65 to 97.47 deg (Sun and Moon)
%   and the LTAN of the pair drifts from 10:30 to about 09:12 over the 5 years; with
%   HoldSSO = 1 the LTAN of the pair centre stays within 0.9 min. Without any
%   control the same pair (started in its slots, ControlOn = 0) loses 7.8 km of
%   altitude in year 1, leaves the along-track corridor after 152 days and the
%   N-amplitude band after 702 days, and the LTAN slips by about 30 min.

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Spacecraft
%----------------------------------------

% Both satellites are defined by mean (Brouwer-Lyddane) elements in the Earth
% true-of-date frame. The orbit and formation geometry are set at the start of
% the mission sequence from the design parameters.
Create Spacecraft Sat1;
Sat1.DateFormat       = UTCGregorian;
Sat1.Epoch            = '01 Jan 2027 00:00:00.000';
Sat1.CoordinateSystem = EarthTOD;
Sat1.DisplayStateType = BrouwerMeanShort;
Sat1.BrouwerShortSMA  = 6938.137;
Sat1.BrouwerShortECC  = 0.0012;
Sat1.BrouwerShortINC  = 97.7876;
Sat1.BrouwerShortRAAN = 258.7256;
Sat1.BrouwerShortAOP  = 90;
Sat1.BrouwerShortMA   = 0;
Sat1.DryMass          = 395;
Sat1.Cd               = 3.0;
Sat1.Cr               = 1.3;
Sat1.DragArea         = 4.5;
Sat1.SRPArea          = 4.5;
Sat1.Tanks            = {Tank1};
Sat1.Thrusters        = {FeepT1, FeepNp1, FeepNm1, FeepR1};
Sat1.PowerSystem      = FeepPower;

Create Spacecraft Sat2;
Sat2.DateFormat       = UTCGregorian;
Sat2.Epoch            = '01 Jan 2027 00:00:00.000';
Sat2.CoordinateSystem = EarthTOD;
Sat2.DisplayStateType = BrouwerMeanShort;
Sat2.BrouwerShortSMA  = 6938.137;
Sat2.BrouwerShortECC  = 0.0012;
Sat2.BrouwerShortINC  = 97.7876;
Sat2.BrouwerShortRAAN = 258.7256;
Sat2.BrouwerShortAOP  = 90;
Sat2.BrouwerShortMA   = 0;
Sat2.DryMass          = 395;
Sat2.Cd               = 3.0;
Sat2.Cr               = 1.3;
Sat2.DragArea         = 4.5;
Sat2.SRPArea          = 4.5;
Sat2.Tanks            = {Tank2};
Sat2.Thrusters        = {FeepT2, FeepNp2, FeepNm2, FeepR2};
Sat2.PowerSystem      = FeepPower;

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Hardware Components
%----------------------------------------

% Idealised constant power source, so that eclipses and sun angle never limit
% the FEEP thrust (the thrusters are modelled as ConstantThrustAndIsp).
Create NuclearPowerSystem FeepPower;
FeepPower.InitialMaxPower = 1;
FeepPower.AnnualDecayRate = 0;
FeepPower.Margin          = 0;
FeepPower.BusCoeff1       = 0.1;
FeepPower.BusCoeff2       = 0;
FeepPower.BusCoeff3       = 0;

Create ElectricTank Tank1;
Tank1.AllowNegativeFuelMass = false;
Tank1.FuelMass              = 5;

Create ElectricTank Tank2;
Tank2.AllowNegativeFuelMass = false;
Tank2.FuelMass              = 5;

% The out-of-plane thrusters fire along +/-Y, the default SecondDirection of GMAT
% hardware, which makes it print a harmless 'collinear' message at start-up; the
% SecondDirection is set to X to avoid that. It does not affect the thrust.
%
% Satellite 1: prograde tangential thruster and +N / -N out-of-plane thrusters.
% Thrust directions are fixed in the VNB frame (V = velocity, N = orbit normal).
% ConstantThrust is in Newton. It must match the ThrustN variable below.
Create ElectricThruster FeepT1;
FeepT1.CoordinateSystem   = Local;
FeepT1.Origin             = Earth;
FeepT1.Axes               = VNB;
FeepT1.ThrustDirection1   = 1;
FeepT1.ThrustDirection2   = 0;
FeepT1.ThrustDirection3   = 0;
FeepT1.DutyCycle          = 0;
FeepT1.DecrementMass      = true;
FeepT1.Tank               = {Tank1};
FeepT1.GravitationalAccel = 9.80665;
FeepT1.ThrustModel        = ConstantThrustAndIsp;
FeepT1.MaximumUsablePower = 0.5;
FeepT1.MinimumUsablePower = 0.001;
FeepT1.ConstantThrust     = 0.001;
FeepT1.Isp                = 2800;

Create ElectricThruster FeepNp1;
FeepNp1.CoordinateSystem   = Local;
FeepNp1.Origin             = Earth;
FeepNp1.Axes               = VNB;
FeepNp1.ThrustDirection1   = 0;
FeepNp1.ThrustDirection2   = 1;
FeepNp1.ThrustDirection3   = 0;
FeepNp1.SecondDirectionX    = 1;
FeepNp1.SecondDirectionY    = 0;
FeepNp1.SecondDirectionZ    = 0;
FeepNp1.DutyCycle          = 0;
FeepNp1.DecrementMass      = true;
FeepNp1.Tank               = {Tank1};
FeepNp1.GravitationalAccel = 9.80665;
FeepNp1.ThrustModel        = ConstantThrustAndIsp;
FeepNp1.MaximumUsablePower = 0.5;
FeepNp1.MinimumUsablePower = 0.001;
FeepNp1.ConstantThrust     = 0.001;
FeepNp1.Isp                = 2800;

Create ElectricThruster FeepNm1;
FeepNm1.CoordinateSystem   = Local;
FeepNm1.Origin             = Earth;
FeepNm1.Axes               = VNB;
FeepNm1.ThrustDirection1   = 0;
FeepNm1.ThrustDirection2   = -1;
FeepNm1.ThrustDirection3   = 0;
FeepNm1.SecondDirectionX    = 1;
FeepNm1.SecondDirectionY    = 0;
FeepNm1.SecondDirectionZ    = 0;
FeepNm1.DutyCycle          = 0;
FeepNm1.DecrementMass      = true;
FeepNm1.Tank               = {Tank1};
FeepNm1.GravitationalAccel = 9.80665;
FeepNm1.ThrustModel        = ConstantThrustAndIsp;
FeepNm1.MaximumUsablePower = 0.5;
FeepNm1.MinimumUsablePower = 0.001;
FeepNm1.ConstantThrust     = 0.001;
FeepNm1.Isp                = 2800;

% Satellite 2: identical thruster set
Create ElectricThruster FeepT2;
FeepT2.CoordinateSystem   = Local;
FeepT2.Origin             = Earth;
FeepT2.Axes               = VNB;
FeepT2.ThrustDirection1   = 1;
FeepT2.ThrustDirection2   = 0;
FeepT2.ThrustDirection3   = 0;
FeepT2.DutyCycle          = 0;
FeepT2.DecrementMass      = true;
FeepT2.Tank               = {Tank2};
FeepT2.GravitationalAccel = 9.80665;
FeepT2.ThrustModel        = ConstantThrustAndIsp;
FeepT2.MaximumUsablePower = 0.5;
FeepT2.MinimumUsablePower = 0.001;
FeepT2.ConstantThrust     = 0.001;
FeepT2.Isp                = 2800;

Create ElectricThruster FeepNp2;
FeepNp2.CoordinateSystem   = Local;
FeepNp2.Origin             = Earth;
FeepNp2.Axes               = VNB;
FeepNp2.ThrustDirection1   = 0;
FeepNp2.ThrustDirection2   = 1;
FeepNp2.ThrustDirection3   = 0;
FeepNp2.SecondDirectionX    = 1;
FeepNp2.SecondDirectionY    = 0;
FeepNp2.SecondDirectionZ    = 0;
FeepNp2.DutyCycle          = 0;
FeepNp2.DecrementMass      = true;
FeepNp2.Tank               = {Tank2};
FeepNp2.GravitationalAccel = 9.80665;
FeepNp2.ThrustModel        = ConstantThrustAndIsp;
FeepNp2.MaximumUsablePower = 0.5;
FeepNp2.MinimumUsablePower = 0.001;
FeepNp2.ConstantThrust     = 0.001;
FeepNp2.Isp                = 2800;

Create ElectricThruster FeepNm2;
FeepNm2.CoordinateSystem   = Local;
FeepNm2.Origin             = Earth;
FeepNm2.Axes               = VNB;
FeepNm2.ThrustDirection1   = 0;
FeepNm2.ThrustDirection2   = -1;
FeepNm2.ThrustDirection3   = 0;
FeepNm2.SecondDirectionX    = 1;
FeepNm2.SecondDirectionY    = 0;
FeepNm2.SecondDirectionZ    = 0;
FeepNm2.DutyCycle          = 0;
FeepNm2.DecrementMass      = true;
FeepNm2.Tank               = {Tank2};
FeepNm2.GravitationalAccel = 9.80665;
FeepNm2.ThrustModel        = ConstantThrustAndIsp;
FeepNm2.MaximumUsablePower = 0.5;
FeepNm2.MinimumUsablePower = 0.001;
FeepNm2.ConstantThrust     = 0.001;
FeepNm2.Isp                = 2800;


% Retrograde thrusters, used ONLY for the end-of-life clearance and disposal
% (the operational control above is prograde + out-of-plane).
Create ElectricThruster FeepR1;
FeepR1.CoordinateSystem   = Local;
FeepR1.Origin             = Earth;
FeepR1.Axes               = VNB;
FeepR1.ThrustDirection1   = -1;
FeepR1.ThrustDirection2   = 0;
FeepR1.ThrustDirection3   = 0;
FeepR1.DutyCycle          = 0;
FeepR1.DecrementMass      = true;
FeepR1.Tank               = {Tank1};
FeepR1.GravitationalAccel = 9.80665;
FeepR1.ThrustModel        = ConstantThrustAndIsp;
FeepR1.MaximumUsablePower = 0.5;
FeepR1.MinimumUsablePower = 0.001;
FeepR1.ConstantThrust     = 0.001;
FeepR1.Isp                = 2800;
Create ElectricThruster FeepR2;
FeepR2.CoordinateSystem   = Local;
FeepR2.Origin             = Earth;
FeepR2.Axes               = VNB;
FeepR2.ThrustDirection1   = -1;
FeepR2.ThrustDirection2   = 0;
FeepR2.ThrustDirection3   = 0;
FeepR2.DutyCycle          = 0;
FeepR2.DecrementMass      = true;
FeepR2.Tank               = {Tank2};
FeepR2.GravitationalAccel = 9.80665;
FeepR2.ThrustModel        = ConstantThrustAndIsp;
FeepR2.MaximumUsablePower = 0.5;
FeepR2.MinimumUsablePower = 0.001;
FeepR2.ConstantThrust     = 0.001;
FeepR2.Isp                = 2800;

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Burns
%----------------------------------------

Create FiniteBurn Burn1;
Burn1.Thrusters = {FeepT1, FeepNp1, FeepNm1, FeepR1};

Create FiniteBurn Burn2;
Burn2.Thrusters = {FeepT2, FeepNp2, FeepNm2, FeepR2};

%----------------------------------------
%---------- ForceModels
%----------------------------------------

% 8x8 EGM96, Sun and Moon point masses, SRP, NRLMSISE-00 drag driven by the
% Schatten (MSFC) solar-cycle prediction. AD10 (EOP-FM/2024-07-177, 5.9) asks for
% the 95th percentile of F10.7 and Ap for the beginning of life and the nominal
% operations (here the Schatten +2 sigma prediction, 'PlusTwoSigma') and for the
% 50th percentile for the end-of-life operations ('Nominal', see EolFM below).
% Use 'Nominal' for the 50th percentile or 'MinusTwoSigma', and SchattenTimingModel
% 'EarlyCycle' / 'LateCycle', for other solar-activity scenarios. Replace
% SchattenPredict.txt by the project's MSFC prediction file when there is one.
Create ForceModel FormationFM;
FormationFM.CentralBody                      = Earth;
FormationFM.PrimaryBodies                    = {Earth};
FormationFM.PointMasses                      = {Sun, Luna};
FormationFM.SRP                              = On;
FormationFM.RelativisticCorrection           = Off;
FormationFM.ErrorControl                     = RSSStep;
FormationFM.GravityField.Earth.Degree        = 8;
FormationFM.GravityField.Earth.Order         = 8;
FormationFM.GravityField.Earth.PotentialFile = 'EGM96.cof';
FormationFM.GravityField.Earth.TideModel     = 'None';
FormationFM.SRP.Flux                         = 1367;
FormationFM.SRP.SRPModel                     = Spherical;
FormationFM.SRP.Nominal_Sun                  = 149597870.691;
FormationFM.Drag.AtmosphereModel             = NRLMSISE00;
FormationFM.Drag.HistoricWeatherSource       = 'ConstantFluxAndGeoMag';
FormationFM.Drag.PredictedWeatherSource      = 'SchattenFile';
FormationFM.Drag.SchattenFile                = 'SchattenPredict.txt';
FormationFM.Drag.SchattenErrorModel          = 'PlusTwoSigma';
FormationFM.Drag.SchattenTimingModel         = 'NominalCycle';
FormationFM.Drag.F107                        = 150;
FormationFM.Drag.F107A                       = 150;
FormationFM.Drag.MagneticIndex               = 3;

% End-of-life force model: 50th percentile solar activity (AD10 5.9, ESSB-ST-U-007
% 6.2.g), 4x4 gravity (the lifetime is driven by drag, not by the tesseral terms).
Create ForceModel EolFM;
EolFM.CentralBody                      = Earth;
EolFM.PrimaryBodies                    = {Earth};
EolFM.PointMasses                      = {Sun, Luna};
EolFM.SRP                              = On;
EolFM.RelativisticCorrection           = Off;
EolFM.ErrorControl                     = RSSStep;
EolFM.GravityField.Earth.Degree        = 4;
EolFM.GravityField.Earth.Order         = 4;
EolFM.GravityField.Earth.PotentialFile = 'EGM96.cof';
EolFM.GravityField.Earth.TideModel     = 'None';
EolFM.SRP.Flux                         = 1367;
EolFM.SRP.SRPModel                     = Spherical;
EolFM.SRP.Nominal_Sun                  = 149597870.691;
EolFM.Drag.AtmosphereModel             = NRLMSISE00;
EolFM.Drag.HistoricWeatherSource       = 'ConstantFluxAndGeoMag';
EolFM.Drag.PredictedWeatherSource      = 'SchattenFile';
EolFM.Drag.SchattenFile                = 'SchattenPredict.txt';
EolFM.Drag.SchattenErrorModel          = 'Nominal';
EolFM.Drag.SchattenTimingModel         = 'NominalCycle';
EolFM.Drag.F107                        = 150;
EolFM.Drag.F107A                       = 150;
EolFM.Drag.MagneticIndex               = 3;

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Propagators
%----------------------------------------

Create Propagator FormationProp;
FormationProp.FM                       = FormationFM;
FormationProp.Type                     = PrinceDormand78;
FormationProp.InitialStepSize          = 60;
FormationProp.Accuracy                 = 1e-10;
FormationProp.MinStep                  = 0.001;
FormationProp.MaxStep                  = 300;
FormationProp.MaxStepAttempts          = 50;
FormationProp.StopIfAccuracyIsViolated = true;

Create Propagator EolProp;
EolProp.FM                       = EolFM;
EolProp.Type                     = PrinceDormand78;
EolProp.InitialStepSize          = 60;
EolProp.Accuracy                 = 1e-9;
EolProp.MinStep                  = 0.001;
EolProp.MaxStep                  = 600;
EolProp.MaxStepAttempts          = 50;
EolProp.StopIfAccuracyIsViolated = false;

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Coordinate Systems
%----------------------------------------

% Earth true-of-date equator. The mean elements (inclination, RAAN) used for
% control are referred to it: relative to the J2000 equator the inclination
% oscillates by ~0.1 deg with the precession accumulated since 2000, which
% would be mistaken for a real drift.
Create CoordinateSystem EarthTOD;
EarthTOD.Origin = Earth;
EarthTOD.Axes   = TODEq;

% RTN frame centred on Sat1: X = radial, Y = along-track, Z = orbit normal.
% Sat2.Sat1RTN.Y is the along-track separation, Sat2.Sat1RTN.Z the normal one.
Create CoordinateSystem Sat1RTN;
Sat1RTN.Origin    = Sat1;
Sat1RTN.Axes      = ObjectReferenced;
Sat1RTN.XAxis     = R;
Sat1RTN.ZAxis     = N;
Sat1RTN.Primary   = Earth;
Sat1RTN.Secondary = Sat1;

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Variables
%----------------------------------------

% Design parameters
Create Variable ControlOn MissionDays MissionSecs MissionOrbits CycleOrbits CycleSecs;
Create Variable aRef eRef iRef aopRef raanRef;
Create Variable NAmp T0 TLow THigh TCenter VdT VtolT kappaT;
Create Variable ThrustN Isp0 g0;

% Controller tuning
Create Variable tauA tauI iDead iTol ffInit diBias eOmTol eOmRel iDead2 iAim aimSign startC diRem1 diRem2 absRem1 absRem2;

% Constants
Create Variable muE ReE J2E PiC;

% Initial geometry
Create Variable iRad sI cI dRaanRad dRaan du0;

% Time, cycle and orbit bookkeeping
Create Variable tNext tSim tDays nCyc nOrbCycle orbT orbDone orbNext finished iOrb iSeg;
Create Variable uTarget uNow1 uNow2 uErr uDotNom TnNom;

% Cycle measurements and commands (suffix 1 / 2 = satellite)
Create Variable aM1 aM2 iM1 iM2 raanM1 raanM2 eM1 eM2 aAvg1 aAvg2 iAvg1 iAvg2;
Create Variable sumA1 sumA2 sumI1 sumI2 aTmp iTmp;
Create Variable Trel Nrel Rrel Rng ANamp dRaanM dRaanDeg diM;
Create Variable diCmd iTgt2 eOm absEo nOmEv HoldSSO iDeadRel iAimRel;
Create Variable Tprev TdotM TdotDes dTe dANeed relMode doRel absTe CyclePrev dACmd aTgt1 aTgt2;
Create Variable nM1 nM2 uDot1 uDot2 uDotD1 uDotD2 sM1 sM2 s2M1 s2M2 vCirc1 vCirc2;
Create Variable mass1 mass2 fMax1 fMax2;
Create Variable delta1 delta2 absD1 absD2 ff1 ff2 fCmd1 fCmd2 dutyT1 dutyT2 Kp1 Kp2;
Create Variable diErr1 diErr2 absDi1 absDi2 camp1 camp2 sAsc1 sAsc2 dutyN1 dutyN2 diMax1 diMax2;
Create Variable aop1 aop2 ta1 ta2 uTmp1 uTmp2 cu1 cu2 s01 s02 tb1 tb2 segT sg;
Create Variable dvT1 dvN1 dvT2 dvN2 dvTot mProp1 mProp2 dvRkt1 dvRkt2 m01 m02;
Create Variable dutySumT1 dutySumT2 dutyMaxT1 dutyMaxT2 campCyc1 campCyc2;

% Compliance statistics
Create Variable TMin TMax ANMin ANMax RngMin dAMax1 dAMax2 nOutT nOutN nRel dEp absEp epMax;

% Acquisition (both satellites start at the same place)
Create Variable AcqOn VAcq TLeadAcq diAcq acq acqT acqN zeroA tAcq dvAcq1 dvAcq2 dvAcqTot;
Create Variable LaunchDelayDays A1Mod0 raanTmp EolOn dAClear HDisp CdEol LifeMaxDays HReentry;
Create Variable aEol1 aEol2 aClearT1 aClearT2 aDispT aNow1 aNow2 iEol nNowE dAday dRemE dutyE dvStep t0Eol;
Create Variable dvClr1 dvClr2 dvDisp1 dvDisp2 life1 life2 hEnd1 hEnd2 mEolA1 mEolA2 mEolB1 mEolB2;
Create Variable massPre massPost aPrev aLoC fracC mPropEol1 mPropEol2 dvRktEol1 dvRktEol2;
Create Variable dvAcqT1 dvAcqN1 dvAcqT2 dvAcqN2 dvNo1 dvNo2 dvNf1 dvNf2 dvN1pre dvN2pre dNinc1 dNinc2;
Create Variable relRem kOm vCircA diMaxA diNow absDiNow diEnd tRampD dFut dPred TStopUp useAbs;

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Subscribers
%----------------------------------------

Create ReportFile DailyReport;
DailyReport.Filename       = 'FormationSSO_FEEP_Daily.txt';
DailyReport.Precision      = 10;
DailyReport.WriteHeaders   = true;
DailyReport.LeftJustify    = On;
DailyReport.ZeroFill       = Off;
DailyReport.FixedWidth     = true;
DailyReport.ColumnWidth    = 20;
DailyReport.WriteReport    = true;

Create ReportFile SummaryReport;
SummaryReport.Filename     = 'FormationSSO_FEEP_Summary.txt';
SummaryReport.Precision    = 8;
SummaryReport.WriteHeaders = true;
SummaryReport.LeftJustify  = On;
SummaryReport.ZeroFill     = Off;
SummaryReport.FixedWidth   = true;
SummaryReport.ColumnWidth  = 20;
SummaryReport.WriteReport  = true;

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Mission Sequence
%----------------------------------------

BeginMissionSequence;

%---------------------------------------------------------------
%  Design parameters (edit here)
%---------------------------------------------------------------
ControlOn   = 1;         % 1 = controlled, 0 = free drift (no thrust at all)
HoldSSO     = 0;         % 1 = also hold the sun-synchronous inclination (and so the LTAN)
                         % 0 = no absolute inclination control: the orbit plane may
                         %     drift, only the formation geometry is kept
MissionDays = 1826;      % 5 years incl. one leap day (2028)
CycleOrbits = 15;        % control cycle = 15 nodal periods (~1.000 day)

% Reference mean orbit (Brouwer-Lyddane "short" mean elements, true-of-date)
aRef    = 6938.137;      % km, 560 km altitude
eRef    = 0.0012;        % frozen-orbit eccentricity
aopRef  = 90;            % deg, frozen-orbit argument of perigee
iRef    = 97.653;        % deg, tuned for exactly sun-synchronous nodal rate
raanRef = 258.7256;      % deg, LTAN 10:30 at 01 Jan 2027 (centre of the pair)

% Formation requirement (Sat2 relative to Sat1, RTN)
NAmp    = 200;           % km, normal separation amplitude
T0      = 550;           % km, initial along-track separation (mid corridor)
TLow    = 350;           % km, reverse drift below this (requirement: 300)
THigh   = 750;           % km, reverse drift above this (requirement: 800)
TCenter = 550;           % km, stop the reversal drift when back at this value
VdT     = 1.5;           % km/day, drift rate used to come back from a limit
VtolT   = 0.4;           % km/day, tolerance on the commanded drift rate
kappaT  = 0.3;           % fraction of the needed SMA change commanded per cycle

% FEEP assumptions (ThrustN must equal ConstantThrust above, Isp0 the Isp)
ThrustN = 0.001;         % N per thruster (1 mN FEEP, maximum thrust)
Isp0    = 2800;          % s
g0      = 9.80665;       % m/s^2, standard gravity (AD10), same as the thrusters' GravitationalAccel

% Controller tuning
tauA    = 129600;        % s, altitude loop time constant (1.5 day)
tauI    = 1296000;       % s, altitude loop integral time (15 day, overdamped)
ffInit  = 1.0e-7;        % m/s^2, first guess of the drag make-up acceleration
iDead   = 0.01;          % deg, start an inclination campaign above this error
iTol    = 0.0005;        % deg, a campaign ends when the commanded change left is below this
iAim    = 0.005;         % deg, a campaign aims this far past the reference (against the drift)
iDeadRel = 0.001;        % deg, HoldSSO = 0: Sat2 corrects when its inclination differs
                         %      from Sat1's by more than this
iAimRel = 0.0005;        % deg, ... and aims this far past Sat1's inclination
eOmTol  = 0.04;          % deg, tolerated drift of the RAAN offset (about 5 km of N amplitude)
diBias  = 0.004;         % deg, differential inclination used to steer the RAAN offset back

% Acquisition of the formation (only with ControlOn = 1)
AcqOn    = 1;            % 1 = both satellites start at the same position and the formation
                         %     is built first by a phasing manoeuvre; 0 = start in formation
VAcq     = 10;           % km/day, along-track drift rate during the acquisition
TLeadAcq = 80;           % km, stop the drift this far before TCenter (the drift decays with drag and overshoots by about this much)
diAcq    = 0.1;          % deg, inclination offset of Sat2 over Sat1 that drives the RAAN
                         %      offset apart (Sat1 goes down and Sat2 up by half of it)

% Launch date (AD10 5.5: also assess launch delays of up to 5 years). The epoch
% is moved by LaunchDelayDays and the node follows the mean Sun, so the LTAN
% is kept; the solar activity (Schatten file) of the new dates is used.
LaunchDelayDays = 0;     % days after 01 Jan 2027

% End-of-life operations (AD10 6.3, ESSB-ST-U-007 5.4.2.3). After the mission both
% satellites are lowered with their retrograde thrusters (continuous full thrust):
% first the clearance of the operational orbit (SMA drop of at least 5 km), then
% the disposal to an orbit whose natural decay is shorter than 5 years. The
% lifetime is then verified by propagating with Cd 2.2 and the 50th percentile of
% the solar activity (EolFM) until re-entry (HReentry) or LifeMaxDays.
EolOn       = 1;         % 0 = stop at the end of the mission
dAClear     = 5;         % km, AD10: minimum SMA drop to clear the operational orbit
HDisp       = 450;       % km, mean altitude of the disposal orbit (natural decay 4.7 years at worst including the thrusting descent, see the lifetime sweep)
CdEol       = 2.2;       % AD10: Cd for the end-of-life operations
LifeMaxDays = 1826;      % days, 5 years (ESSB-ST-U-007 5.4.2.3)
HReentry    = 120;       % km, altitude taken as re-entry

% Constants (EGM96)
muE = 398600.4415;
ReE = 6378.1363;
J2E = 1.08262668e-3;
PiC = 3.14159265358979;

%---------------------------------------------------------------
%  Initial formation geometry
%---------------------------------------------------------------
MissionSecs = MissionDays * 86400;
% Launch date: move the epoch of both satellites and the node with the mean Sun
A1Mod0 = Sat1.A1ModJulian;
Sat1.A1ModJulian = A1Mod0 + LaunchDelayDays;
Sat2.A1ModJulian = A1Mod0 + LaunchDelayDays;
raanTmp = raanRef + 0.9856474 * LaunchDelayDays;
raanRef = mod(raanTmp, 360);
iRad     = degToRad(iRef);
sI       = sin(iRad);
cI       = cos(iRad);
dRaanRad = NAmp / (aRef * sI);
dRaan    = radToDeg(dRaanRad);
du0      = radToDeg(T0 / aRef) - dRaan * cI;
acq      = 0;
If AcqOn == 1
   If ControlOn == 1
      acq = 1;
   EndIf;
EndIf;

Sat1.BrouwerShortSMA  = aRef;
Sat1.BrouwerShortECC  = eRef;
Sat1.BrouwerShortINC  = iRef;
Sat1.BrouwerShortRAAN = raanRef - 0.5 * dRaan;
Sat1.BrouwerShortAOP  = aopRef;
Sat1.BrouwerShortMA   = 0;

Sat2.BrouwerShortSMA  = aRef;
Sat2.BrouwerShortECC  = eRef;
Sat2.BrouwerShortINC  = iRef;
Sat2.BrouwerShortRAAN = raanRef + 0.5 * dRaan;
Sat2.BrouwerShortAOP  = aopRef;
Sat2.BrouwerShortMA   = du0;
% Acquisition start: both satellites are released at the same position, on the
% node of the centre of the formation. The acquisition moves the nodes of the two
% satellites apart symmetrically, to raanRef -/+ dRaan/2, so the LTAN of the pair
% centre stays at the reference.
If acq == 1
   Sat1.BrouwerShortRAAN = raanRef;
   Sat2.BrouwerShortRAAN = raanRef;
   Sat2.BrouwerShortMA   = 0;
EndIf;

%---------------------------------------------------------------
%  Initialise controller state and statistics
%---------------------------------------------------------------
tSim = 0;
nCyc = 0;
orbDone = 0;
finished = 0;
dACmd = 0;
diCmd = 0;
nOmEv = 0;
relMode = 0;
Tprev = T0;
If acq == 1
   Tprev = 0;
EndIf;
acqT = acq;
acqN = acq;
dvAcqT1 = 0;
dvAcqN1 = 0;
dvAcqT2 = 0;
dvAcqN2 = 0;
dvNo1 = 0;
dvNo2 = 0;
dvNf1 = 0;
dvNf2 = 0;
zeroA = 0;
tAcq = 0;
dvAcq1 = 0;
dvAcq2 = 0;
dvAcqTot = 0;
CyclePrev = 86400;
ff1 = ffInit;
ff2 = ffInit;
camp1 = 0;
camp2 = 0;
diRem1 = 0;
diRem2 = 0;
dvT1 = 0;
dvN1 = 0;
dvT2 = 0;
dvN2 = 0;
dutySumT1 = 0;
dutySumT2 = 0;
dutyMaxT1 = 0;
dutyMaxT2 = 0;
campCyc1 = 0;
campCyc2 = 0;
TMin = 1e9;
TMax = -1e9;
ANMin = 1e9;
ANMax = -1e9;
RngMin = 1e9;
dAMax1 = 0;
dAMax2 = 0;
nOutT = 0;
nOutN = 0;
nRel = 0;
epMax = 0;
m01 = Sat1.TotalMass;
m02 = Sat2.TotalMass;

% Mean elements fed to the controller are averaged over the 15 orbits of the
% previous cycle (sampled once per orbit at the same argument of latitude).
% This removes the tesseral-harmonic short-period terms (tens of metres in SMA),
% which would otherwise look like noise to the controller.
aAvg1 = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
aAvg2 = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
iAvg1 = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;
iAvg2 = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;

% Argument of latitude at which the cycle starts, kept constant by adjusting
% the length of each cycle. Mission length in orbits from the nominal period.
aop1 = Sat1.EarthTOD.AOP;
ta1  = Sat1.Earth.TA;
uTmp1 = aop1 + ta1;
uTarget = mod(uTmp1, 360);
nM1     = sqrt(muE / (aRef*aRef*aRef));
s2M1    = sI * sI;
uDotNom = nM1 * (1 + J2E * (ReE/aRef) * (ReE/aRef) * (4.5 - 6 * s2M1));
TnNom   = 2 * PiC / uDotNom;
% d(RAAN rate)/d(inclination) in deg/day per deg, used to plan the acquisition
kOm     = 1.5 * J2E * (ReE/aRef) * (ReE/aRef) * nM1 * sI * 86400;
MissionOrbits = fix(MissionSecs / TnNom);

While finished == 0

   %------------------------------------------------------------
   %  1. Measurements: relative RTN state, mean elements for the log
   %------------------------------------------------------------
   tDays  = tSim / 86400;
   aM1    = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
   aM2    = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
   iM1    = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;
   iM2    = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;
   raanM1 = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortRAAN;
   raanM2 = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortRAAN;
   eM1    = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortECC;
   eM2    = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortECC;
   % The satellites are propagated one after the other for the same time, so
   % they are at the same epoch whenever the RTN state is read; epMax checks it.
   dEp    = (Sat2.A1ModJulian - Sat1.A1ModJulian) * 86400;
   absEp  = abs(dEp);
   If absEp > epMax
      epMax = absEp;
   EndIf;
   Rrel   = Sat2.Sat1RTN.X;
   Trel   = Sat2.Sat1RTN.Y;
   Nrel   = Sat2.Sat1RTN.Z;
   Rng    = sqrt(Rrel*Rrel + Trel*Trel + Nrel*Nrel);
   mass1  = Sat1.TotalMass;
   mass2  = Sat2.TotalMass;

   % Normal-separation amplitude from the mean-element differences
   dRaanM = raanM2 - raanM1;
   If dRaanM > 180
      dRaanM = dRaanM - 360;
   EndIf;
   If dRaanM < -180
      dRaanM = dRaanM + 360;
   EndIf;
   dRaanDeg = dRaanM;
   diM    = degToRad(iAvg2 - iAvg1);
   dRaanM = degToRad(dRaanM);
   sM1    = sin(degToRad(iAvg1));
   ANamp  = aAvg1 * sqrt(diM*diM + sM1*sM1*dRaanM*dRaanM);

   % End of the acquisition: drift stopped, node offset reached, inclination offset removed
   diNow    = iAvg2 - iAvg1;
   absDiNow = abs(diNow);
   diEnd    = 0.1 * diAcq;
   If acq == 1
      If acqT == 0
         If acqN == 0
            If camp1 == 0
            If camp2 == 0
              If absDiNow < diEnd
               acq = 0;
               tAcq = tDays;
               dvAcq1 = dvT1 + dvN1;
               dvAcq2 = dvT2 + dvN2;
               dvAcqTot = dvAcq1 + dvAcq2;
               dvAcqT1 = dvT1;
               dvAcqN1 = dvN1;
               dvAcqT2 = dvT2;
               dvAcqN2 = dvN2;
              EndIf;
            EndIf;
            EndIf;
         EndIf;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;

   % Statistics (compliance is counted after the acquisition)
   If acq == 0
   If Trel < TMin
      TMin = Trel;
   EndIf;
   If Trel > TMax
      TMax = Trel;
   EndIf;
   If ANamp < ANMin
      ANMin = ANamp;
   EndIf;
   If ANamp > ANMax
      ANMax = ANamp;
   EndIf;
   If Rng < RngMin
      RngMin = Rng;
   EndIf;
   If Trel < 300
      nOutT = nOutT + 1;
   EndIf;
   If Trel > 800
      nOutT = nOutT + 1;
   EndIf;
   If ANamp < 180
      nOutN = nOutN + 1;
   EndIf;
   If ANamp > 220
      nOutN = nOutN + 1;
   EndIf;
   EndIf;

   %------------------------------------------------------------
   %  2. Cycle length: 15 nodal periods, phase locked to Sat1
   %------------------------------------------------------------
   orbNext = orbDone + CycleOrbits;
   nOrbCycle = CycleOrbits;
   If orbNext > MissionOrbits
      nOrbCycle = MissionOrbits - orbDone;
   EndIf;
   If nOrbCycle < 1
      nOrbCycle = 1;
   EndIf;
   nM1     = sqrt(muE / (aAvg1*aAvg1*aAvg1));
   nM2     = sqrt(muE / (aAvg2*aAvg2*aAvg2));
   sM1     = sin(degToRad(iAvg1));
   sM2     = sin(degToRad(iAvg2));
   s2M1    = sM1 * sM1;
   s2M2    = sM2 * sM2;
   uDot1   = nM1 * (1 + J2E * (ReE/aAvg1) * (ReE/aAvg1) * (4.5 - 6 * s2M1));
   uDot2   = nM2 * (1 + J2E * (ReE/aAvg2) * (ReE/aAvg2) * (4.5 - 6 * s2M2));
   uDotD1  = radToDeg(uDot1);
   uDotD2  = radToDeg(uDot2);
   aop1    = Sat1.EarthTOD.AOP;
   ta1     = Sat1.Earth.TA;
   uTmp1   = aop1 + ta1;
   uNow1   = mod(uTmp1, 360);
   aop2    = Sat2.EarthTOD.AOP;
   ta2     = Sat2.Earth.TA;
   uTmp2   = aop2 + ta2;
   uNow2   = mod(uTmp2, 360);
   uErr    = uTarget - uNow1;
   If uErr > 180
      uErr = uErr - 360;
   EndIf;
   If uErr < -180
      uErr = uErr + 360;
   EndIf;
   CycleSecs = (360 * nOrbCycle + uErr) / uDotD1;
   orbT      = CycleSecs / nOrbCycle;

   %------------------------------------------------------------
   %  3. Relative along-track logic (drift reversal with hysteresis)
   %     Uses the measured drift rate, not absolute SMA differences.
   %------------------------------------------------------------
   TdotM = 0;
   If nCyc > 0
      TdotM = (Trel - Tprev) / (CyclePrev / 86400);
   EndIf;
   TdotDes = 0;
   doRel = 0;
   If relMode == 0
      If Trel > THigh
         relMode = -1;
         doRel = 1;
      EndIf;
      If Trel < TLow
         relMode = 1;
         doRel = 1;
      EndIf;
   Else
      If relMode < 0
         If Trel < TCenter
            relMode = 0;
            doRel = 1;
         EndIf;
      Else
         TStopUp = TCenter;
         If acqT == 1
            TStopUp = TCenter - TLeadAcq;
         EndIf;
         If Trel > TStopUp
            relMode = 0;
            doRel = 1;
            If acqT == 1
               acqT = 0;
               zeroA = 1;
            EndIf;
         EndIf;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;
   If relMode < 0
      TdotDes = -VdT;
   EndIf;
   If relMode > 0
      TdotDes = VdT;
      If acqT == 1
         TdotDes = VAcq;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;
   dTe = TdotDes - TdotM;
   absTe = abs(dTe);
   If relMode ~= 0
      If absTe > VtolT
         doRel = 1;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;
   If doRel == 1
      % T-dot = -1.5 n da  ->  SMA change needed for the commanded drift rate
      dANeed = -dTe / (86400 * 1.5 * nM1);
      dACmd  = dACmd + kappaT * dANeed;
      nRel   = nRel + 1;
      If dACmd > 0.2
         dACmd = 0.2;
      EndIf;
      If dACmd < -0.2
         dACmd = -0.2;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;
   If zeroA == 1
      dACmd = 0;
      zeroA = 0;
   EndIf;
   Tprev     = Trel;
   CyclePrev = CycleSecs;
   % The thrusters are prograde only, so a relative SMA offset is made by
   % raising whichever satellite has to be higher.
   aTgt1 = aRef;
   aTgt2 = aRef;
   If dACmd > 0
      aTgt2 = aRef + dACmd;
   EndIf;
   If dACmd < 0
      aTgt1 = aRef - dACmd;
   EndIf;

   %------------------------------------------------------------
   %  4. Tangential thrust command (PI on mean SMA, prograde only)
   %------------------------------------------------------------
   Kp1    = nM1 / (2 * tauA);
   Kp2    = nM2 / (2 * tauA);
   fMax1  = ThrustN / mass1;
   fMax2  = ThrustN / mass2;

   delta1 = (aAvg1 - aTgt1) * 1000;
   delta2 = (aAvg2 - aTgt2) * 1000;
   absD1  = abs(delta1);
   absD2  = abs(delta2);
   If absD1 > dAMax1
      dAMax1 = absD1;
   EndIf;
   If absD2 > dAMax2
      dAMax2 = absD2;
   EndIf;

   ff1 = ff1 - (Kp1 / tauI) * delta1 * CycleSecs;
   ff2 = ff2 - (Kp2 / tauI) * delta2 * CycleSecs;
   If ff1 < 0
      ff1 = 0;
   EndIf;
   If ff1 > fMax1
      ff1 = fMax1;
   EndIf;
   If ff2 < 0
      ff2 = 0;
   EndIf;
   If ff2 > fMax2
      ff2 = fMax2;
   EndIf;
   fCmd1 = ff1 - Kp1 * delta1;
   fCmd2 = ff2 - Kp2 * delta2;
   If fCmd1 < 0
      fCmd1 = 0;
   EndIf;
   If fCmd1 > fMax1
      fCmd1 = fMax1;
   EndIf;
   If fCmd2 < 0
      fCmd2 = 0;
   EndIf;
   If fCmd2 > fMax2
      fCmd2 = fMax2;
   EndIf;
   dutyT1 = fCmd1 / fMax1;
   dutyT2 = fCmd2 / fMax2;

   %------------------------------------------------------------
   %  5. Inclination (out-of-plane) command with hysteresis
   %------------------------------------------------------------
   % Relative node control. The inclination campaigns of the two satellites are
   % coordinated (both run when Sat1 reaches its limit, or when Sat2 reaches
   % twice the limit), so the two planes keep precessing together. A small differential inclination is applied only
   % if the RAAN offset, hence the N amplitude, has drifted anyway.
   % d(RAAN rate)/d(inc) is positive, so a lower inc of Sat2 shrinks the offset.
   eOm   = dRaanDeg - dRaan;
   eOmRel = 0.25 * eOmTol;
   absEo = abs(eOm);
   If acqN == 1
      % Node acquisition: Sat2 is held diAcq above Sat1 (each satellite moves half of
      % it) so that the node of Sat2 runs ahead.
      % The offset is removed again (taking diNow/diMax cycles, during which the node
      % keeps drifting) as soon as the offset predicted for the end of that ramp
      % reaches the target. The slow trim below removes what is left.
      vCircA = sqrt(muE / aAvg2) * 1000;
      diMaxA = radToDeg((2 / PiC) * (fMax2 / vCircA) * CycleSecs);
      diNow  = iAvg2 - iAvg1;
      tRampD = (diNow / (2 * diMaxA)) * (CycleSecs / 86400);
      dFut   = kOm * diNow * (0.5 * tRampD + 0.5);
      dPred  = eOm + dFut;
      diCmd  = diAcq;
      If dPred > 0
         acqN  = 0;
         diCmd = 0;
      EndIf;
   Else
      If diCmd == 0
         If absEo > eOmTol
            nOmEv = nOmEv + 1;
            diCmd = diBias;
            If eOm > 0
               diCmd = -diBias;
            EndIf;
         EndIf;
      Else
         If absEo < eOmRel
            diCmd = 0;
         EndIf;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;
   % The absolute (sun-synchronous) inclination hold starts after the acquisition
   useAbs = 0;
   If HoldSSO == 1
      If acq == 0
         useAbs = 1;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;
   iTgt2  = iRef + diCmd;
   If useAbs == 0
      iTgt2 = iAvg1 + diCmd;
   EndIf;
   diErr1 = iAvg1 - iRef;
   diErr2 = iAvg2 - iTgt2;
   absDi1 = abs(diErr1);
   absDi2 = abs(diErr2);

   % With HoldSSO = 0 (and during the acquisition) only the inclination of Sat2
   % relative to Sat1 is controlled, and the two satellites share it: each one
   % moves half of the change, in opposite directions, so they use about the
   % same propellant and the common plane is left alone.
   % A campaign is planned open loop: when a limit is reached, the change needed
   % to get to the aim point is commanded over as many cycles as it takes, and
   % the commanded change (not the lagging measurement) is counted down.
   % Both satellites run it together, started by Sat1 reaching iDead, or by
   % Sat2 reaching twice that. The aim point is iAim beyond the reference, on
   % the side opposite to the drift, which halves the number of campaigns.
   iDead2 = 2 * iDead;
   startC = 0;
   aimSign = 0;
   If camp1 == 0
      If camp2 == 0
         If useAbs == 1
            If absDi1 > iDead
               startC = 1;
               aimSign = 1;
               If diErr1 > 0
                  aimSign = -1;
               EndIf;
            EndIf;
            If absDi2 > iDead2
               startC = 1;
               aimSign = 1;
               If diErr2 > 0
                  aimSign = -1;
               EndIf;
            EndIf;
         Else
            % Only the inclination of Sat2 relative to Sat1 is controlled.
            If absDi2 > iDeadRel
               startC = 1;
               aimSign = 1;
               If diErr2 > 0
                  aimSign = -1;
               EndIf;
            EndIf;
         EndIf;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;
   If startC == 1
      If useAbs == 1
         camp1  = 1;
         camp2  = 1;
         diRem1 = -diErr1 + aimSign * iAim;
         diRem2 = -diErr2 + aimSign * iAim;
      Else
         relRem = -diErr2 + aimSign * iAimRel;
         camp1  = 1;
         camp2  = 1;
         diRem1 = -0.5 * relRem;
         diRem2 = 0.5 * relRem;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;

   % Orbit-averaged di/dt of a sign(cos u) out-of-plane thrust: (2/pi) fN / v
   vCirc1 = sqrt(muE / aAvg1) * 1000;
   vCirc2 = sqrt(muE / aAvg2) * 1000;
   diMax1 = radToDeg((2 / PiC) * (fMax1 / vCirc1) * CycleSecs);
   diMax2 = radToDeg((2 / PiC) * (fMax2 / vCirc2) * CycleSecs);
   dutyN1 = 0;
   dutyN2 = 0;
   sAsc1  = 1;
   sAsc2  = 1;
   absRem1 = abs(diRem1);
   absRem2 = abs(diRem2);
   If absRem1 < iTol
      camp1 = 0;
   EndIf;
   If absRem2 < iTol
      camp2 = 0;
   EndIf;
   If camp1 == 1
      dutyN1 = absRem1 / diMax1;
      If dutyN1 > 1
         dutyN1 = 1;
      EndIf;
      If diRem1 < 0
         sAsc1 = -1;
         diRem1 = diRem1 + dutyN1 * diMax1;
      Else
         diRem1 = diRem1 - dutyN1 * diMax1;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;
   If camp2 == 1
      dutyN2 = absRem2 / diMax2;
      If dutyN2 > 1
         dutyN2 = 1;
      EndIf;
      If diRem2 < 0
         sAsc2 = -1;
         diRem2 = diRem2 + dutyN2 * diMax2;
      Else
         diRem2 = diRem2 - dutyN2 * diMax2;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;

   If ControlOn == 0
      dutyT1 = 0;
      dutyT2 = 0;
      dutyN1 = 0;
      dutyN2 = 0;
      camp1  = 0;
      camp2  = 0;
   EndIf;

   %------------------------------------------------------------
   %  6. Log
   %------------------------------------------------------------
   Report DailyReport tDays uNow1 aAvg1 aAvg2 iAvg1 iAvg2 raanM1 raanM2 eM1 eM2 Rrel Trel Nrel Rng ANamp dACmd TdotM diCmd dutyT1 dutyT2 dutyN1 dutyN2 dvT1 dvN1 dvT2 dvN2 mass1 mass2 CycleSecs acq;

   % The last pass (all orbits done) only measures and logs.
   If orbDone >= MissionOrbits
      finished = 1;
   EndIf;

   If finished == 0

      dvN1pre = dvN1;
      dvN2pre = dvN2;
      dutySumT1 = dutySumT1 + dutyT1;
      dutySumT2 = dutySumT2 + dutyT2;
      If dutyT1 > dutyMaxT1
         dutyMaxT1 = dutyT1;
      EndIf;
      If dutyT2 > dutyMaxT2
         dutyMaxT2 = dutyT2;
      EndIf;

      %---------------------------------------------------------
      %  7. Propagate Sat1 one cycle (continuous finite burns)
      %---------------------------------------------------------
      sumA1 = 0;
      sumI1 = 0;
      iOrb  = 1;
      Sat1.FeepT1.DutyCycle  = dutyT1;
      Sat1.FeepNp1.DutyCycle = 0;
      Sat1.FeepNm1.DutyCycle = 0;
      If camp1 == 0
         BeginFiniteBurn Burn1(Sat1);
         While iOrb <= nOrbCycle
            Propagate FormationProp(Sat1) {Sat1.ElapsedSecs = orbT};
            aTmp  = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
            iTmp  = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;
            sumA1 = sumA1 + aTmp;
            sumI1 = sumI1 + iTmp;
            iOrb  = iOrb + 1;
         EndWhile;
         EndFiniteBurn Burn1(Sat1);
      Else
         % Inclination campaign. The out-of-plane thrust follows sign(cos u): it
         % is flipped at the polar points (u = 90 and 270 deg). Each orbit is
         % split into three segments between those switching points.
         campCyc1 = campCyc1 + 1;
         cu1  = cos(degToRad(uNow1));
         s01  = sAsc1;
         If cu1 < 0
            s01 = -sAsc1;
         EndIf;
         tb1  = 450 - uNow1;
         tb1  = mod(tb1, 180);
         tb1  = tb1 / uDotD1;
         While iOrb <= nOrbCycle
            iSeg = 1;
            While iSeg <= 3
               segT = 0.5 * orbT;
               sg   = -s01;
               If iSeg == 1
                  segT = tb1;
                  sg   = s01;
               EndIf;
               If iSeg == 3
                  segT = 0.5 * orbT - tb1;
                  sg   = s01;
               EndIf;
               If segT > 0.5
                  If sg > 0
                     Sat1.FeepNp1.DutyCycle = dutyN1;
                     Sat1.FeepNm1.DutyCycle = 0;
                  Else
                     Sat1.FeepNp1.DutyCycle = 0;
                     Sat1.FeepNm1.DutyCycle = dutyN1;
                  EndIf;
                  BeginFiniteBurn Burn1(Sat1);
                  Propagate FormationProp(Sat1) {Sat1.ElapsedSecs = segT};
                  EndFiniteBurn Burn1(Sat1);
                  dvN1 = dvN1 + dutyN1 * fMax1 * segT;
               EndIf;
               iSeg = iSeg + 1;
            EndWhile;
            aTmp  = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
            iTmp  = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;
            sumA1 = sumA1 + aTmp;
            sumI1 = sumI1 + iTmp;
            iOrb  = iOrb + 1;
         EndWhile;
         Sat1.FeepNp1.DutyCycle = 0;
         Sat1.FeepNm1.DutyCycle = 0;
      EndIf;
      dvT1  = dvT1 + dutyT1 * fMax1 * CycleSecs;
      aAvg1 = sumA1 / nOrbCycle;
      iAvg1 = sumI1 / nOrbCycle;

      %---------------------------------------------------------
      %  8. Propagate Sat2 one cycle
      %---------------------------------------------------------
      sumA2 = 0;
      sumI2 = 0;
      iOrb  = 1;
      Sat2.FeepT2.DutyCycle  = dutyT2;
      Sat2.FeepNp2.DutyCycle = 0;
      Sat2.FeepNm2.DutyCycle = 0;
      If camp2 == 0
         BeginFiniteBurn Burn2(Sat2);
         While iOrb <= nOrbCycle
            Propagate FormationProp(Sat2) {Sat2.ElapsedSecs = orbT};
            aTmp  = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
            iTmp  = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;
            sumA2 = sumA2 + aTmp;
            sumI2 = sumI2 + iTmp;
            iOrb  = iOrb + 1;
         EndWhile;
         EndFiniteBurn Burn2(Sat2);
      Else
         campCyc2 = campCyc2 + 1;
         cu2  = cos(degToRad(uNow2));
         s02  = sAsc2;
         If cu2 < 0
            s02 = -sAsc2;
         EndIf;
         tb2  = 450 - uNow2;
         tb2  = mod(tb2, 180);
         tb2  = tb2 / uDotD2;
         While iOrb <= nOrbCycle
            iSeg = 1;
            While iSeg <= 3
               segT = 0.5 * orbT;
               sg   = -s02;
               If iSeg == 1
                  segT = tb2;
                  sg   = s02;
               EndIf;
               If iSeg == 3
                  segT = 0.5 * orbT - tb2;
                  sg   = s02;
               EndIf;
               If segT > 0.5
                  If sg > 0
                     Sat2.FeepNp2.DutyCycle = dutyN2;
                     Sat2.FeepNm2.DutyCycle = 0;
                  Else
                     Sat2.FeepNp2.DutyCycle = 0;
                     Sat2.FeepNm2.DutyCycle = dutyN2;
                  EndIf;
                  BeginFiniteBurn Burn2(Sat2);
                  Propagate FormationProp(Sat2) {Sat2.ElapsedSecs = segT};
                  EndFiniteBurn Burn2(Sat2);
                  dvN2 = dvN2 + dutyN2 * fMax2 * segT;
               EndIf;
               iSeg = iSeg + 1;
            EndWhile;
            aTmp  = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
            iTmp  = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;
            sumA2 = sumA2 + aTmp;
            sumI2 = sumI2 + iTmp;
            iOrb  = iOrb + 1;
         EndWhile;
         Sat2.FeepNp2.DutyCycle = 0;
         Sat2.FeepNm2.DutyCycle = 0;
      EndIf;
      dvT2  = dvT2 + dutyT2 * fMax2 * CycleSecs;
      aAvg2 = sumA2 / nOrbCycle;
      iAvg2 = sumI2 / nOrbCycle;

      % After the acquisition the normal delta-V is split into the sun-synchronous
      % inclination hold (out-of-plane orbit control) and the formation (Sat2
      % relative to Sat1, node trim).
      dNinc1 = dvN1 - dvN1pre;
      dNinc2 = dvN2 - dvN2pre;
      If acq == 0
         If useAbs == 1
            dvNo1 = dvNo1 + dNinc1;
            dvNo2 = dvNo2 + dNinc2;
         Else
            dvNf1 = dvNf1 + dNinc1;
            dvNf2 = dvNf2 + dNinc2;
         EndIf;
      EndIf;

      tSim    = tSim + CycleSecs;
      orbDone = orbDone + nOrbCycle;
      nCyc    = nCyc + 1;
   EndIf;
EndWhile;

%---------------------------------------------------------------
%  Summary of the mission (beginning of life + nominal operations)
%---------------------------------------------------------------
mProp1    = m01 - Sat1.TotalMass;
mProp2    = m02 - Sat2.TotalMass;
dvRkt1    = Isp0 * g0 * log(m01 / Sat1.TotalMass);
dvRkt2    = Isp0 * g0 * log(m02 / Sat2.TotalMass);
dvTot     = dvT1 + dvN1 + dvT2 + dvN2;
dutySumT1 = dutySumT1 / nCyc;
dutySumT2 = dutySumT2 / nCyc;

%---------------------------------------------------------------
%  End of life: clearance of the operational orbit and disposal
%---------------------------------------------------------------
% Cd 2.2 (AD10 5.2) and the 50th percentile solar activity (EolFM). Each
% satellite is lowered with its retrograde thruster at full thrust, one day at a
% time; the first dAClear km are the clearance, the rest is the disposal. The
% thrust is cut when the mean SMA reaches the disposal orbit, and the natural
% decay from there is propagated until re-entry or LifeMaxDays.
dvClr1  = 0;
dvClr2  = 0;
dvDisp1 = 0;
dvDisp2 = 0;
life1   = 0;
life2   = 0;
hEnd1   = 0;
hEnd2   = 0;
mEolA1  = Sat1.TotalMass;
mEolA2  = Sat2.TotalMass;
mEolB1  = mEolA1;
mEolB2  = mEolA2;
aDispT  = ReE + HDisp;
If EolOn == 1
   If ControlOn == 1
      Sat1.Cd = CdEol;
      Sat2.Cd = CdEol;
      % The operational thrusters keep the duty of the last cycle: switch them off
      Sat1.FeepT1.DutyCycle  = 0;
      Sat1.FeepNp1.DutyCycle = 0;
      Sat1.FeepNm1.DutyCycle = 0;
      Sat2.FeepT2.DutyCycle  = 0;
      Sat2.FeepNp2.DutyCycle = 0;
      Sat2.FeepNm2.DutyCycle = 0;

      aEol1    = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
      aClearT1 = aEol1 - dAClear;
      aNow1    = aEol1;
      iEol     = 0;
      While aNow1 > aDispT & iEol < 600
         nNowE  = sqrt(muE / (aNow1*aNow1*aNow1));
         fMax1  = ThrustN / Sat1.TotalMass;
         dAday  = 2 * fMax1 * 86400 / nNowE / 1000;
         dRemE  = aNow1 - aDispT;
         dutyE  = dRemE / dAday;
         If dutyE > 1
            dutyE = 1;
         EndIf;
         Sat1.FeepR1.DutyCycle = dutyE;
         massPre = Sat1.TotalMass;
         BeginFiniteBurn Burn1(Sat1);
         Propagate EolProp(Sat1) {Sat1.ElapsedSecs = 86400};
         EndFiniteBurn Burn1(Sat1);
         massPost = Sat1.TotalMass;
         dvStep = dutyE * ThrustN * 86400 / (0.5 * (massPre + massPost));
         % share of this day's thrust spent above the clearance level
         aPrev  = aNow1;
         aNow1 = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
         fracC  = 0;
         If aPrev > aClearT1
            aLoC = aNow1;
            If aLoC < aClearT1
               aLoC = aClearT1;
            EndIf;
            fracC = (aPrev - aLoC) / (aPrev - aNow1);
         EndIf;
         dvClr1  = dvClr1 + fracC * dvStep;
         dvDisp1 = dvDisp1 + (1 - fracC) * dvStep;
         iEol  = iEol + 1;
      EndWhile;
      Sat1.FeepR1.DutyCycle = 0;
      mEolB1 = Sat1.TotalMass;

      aEol2    = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
      aClearT2 = aEol2 - dAClear;
      aNow2    = aEol2;
      iEol     = 0;
      While aNow2 > aDispT & iEol < 600
         nNowE  = sqrt(muE / (aNow2*aNow2*aNow2));
         fMax2  = ThrustN / Sat2.TotalMass;
         dAday  = 2 * fMax2 * 86400 / nNowE / 1000;
         dRemE  = aNow2 - aDispT;
         dutyE  = dRemE / dAday;
         If dutyE > 1
            dutyE = 1;
         EndIf;
         Sat2.FeepR2.DutyCycle = dutyE;
         massPre = Sat2.TotalMass;
         BeginFiniteBurn Burn2(Sat2);
         Propagate EolProp(Sat2) {Sat2.ElapsedSecs = 86400};
         EndFiniteBurn Burn2(Sat2);
         massPost = Sat2.TotalMass;
         dvStep = dutyE * ThrustN * 86400 / (0.5 * (massPre + massPost));
         % share of this day's thrust spent above the clearance level
         aPrev  = aNow2;
         aNow2 = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
         fracC  = 0;
         If aPrev > aClearT2
            aLoC = aNow2;
            If aLoC < aClearT2
               aLoC = aClearT2;
            EndIf;
            fracC = (aPrev - aLoC) / (aPrev - aNow2);
         EndIf;
         dvClr2  = dvClr2 + fracC * dvStep;
         dvDisp2 = dvDisp2 + (1 - fracC) * dvStep;
         iEol  = iEol + 1;
      EndWhile;
      Sat2.FeepR2.DutyCycle = 0;
      mEolB2 = Sat2.TotalMass;

      % Natural decay of the disposal orbit (thrusters off)
      t0Eol = Sat1.A1ModJulian;
      Propagate EolProp(Sat1) {Sat1.ElapsedDays = LifeMaxDays, Sat1.Earth.Altitude = HReentry};
      life1 = Sat1.A1ModJulian - t0Eol;
      hEnd1 = Sat1.Earth.Altitude;
      t0Eol = Sat2.A1ModJulian;
      Propagate EolProp(Sat2) {Sat2.ElapsedDays = LifeMaxDays, Sat2.Earth.Altitude = HReentry};
      life2 = Sat2.A1ModJulian - t0Eol;
      hEnd2 = Sat2.Earth.Altitude;
   EndIf;
EndIf;
mPropEol1 = mEolA1 - mEolB1;
mPropEol2 = mEolA2 - mEolB2;
dvRktEol1 = Isp0 * g0 * log(mEolA1 / mEolB1);
dvRktEol2 = Isp0 * g0 * log(mEolA2 / mEolB2);

Report SummaryReport MissionDays tDays nCyc dvT1 dvN1 dvT2 dvN2 dvTot dvRkt1 dvRkt2 mProp1 mProp2;
Report SummaryReport dutySumT1 dutyMaxT1 dutySumT2 dutyMaxT2 campCyc1 campCyc2 dAMax1 dAMax2 nRel nOmEv;
Report SummaryReport TMin TMax ANMin ANMax RngMin nOutT nOutN epMax;
Report SummaryReport tAcq dvAcqT1 dvAcqN1 dvAcqT2 dvAcqN2 dvNo1 dvNo2 dvNf1 dvNf2;
Report SummaryReport dvClr1 dvClr2 dvDisp1 dvDisp2 aDispT life1 life2 hEnd1 hEnd2;
Report SummaryReport mPropEol1 mPropEol2 dvRktEol1 dvRktEol2;
